 Type Staff - Non-Exempt (Hourly) Department Breathitt Veterinary Center Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities Collects and organizes samples for testing, performs laboratory procedures, document and communicate findings. Collects and organizes samples for Virology, Serology, and Molecular Biology testing Utilizes validated laboratory techniques and processes to analyze patient specimens leading to diagnosis Operates sensitive scientific equipment during the analytical process Documents findings in laboratory information management system Recognizes, documents, and provides input to correct substandard quality Develops, reviews, and evaluates processes as necessary Maintain customer confidentiality Clean and sterilize lab section, lab instruments and glassware Order, receive, process and store lab section supplies and equipment Strict adherence to the Quality Management System Participates in university and laboratory committees; additional projects as needed Other duties as assigned. Minimum Education Requirements Bachelor’s Degree required. Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements Ability to quickly adapt to changing circumstances and to coworker personalities Alertness, memory for verbal and written directions and details, analytical ability, and ability to logically plan and organize analytical processes Ability to interpret and verify test results Ability to plan and make decisions often without instruction or supervision Excellent oral and written communication skills Pleasant, proactive personality, ability to handle demanding situations, and work with a team Laboratory techniques, record keeping, and filing procedures; biology and chemistry helpful. Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications One year working experience in an animal diagnostic laboratory Experience using a laboratory information database BS in Biology with courses in Microbiology and Molecular Biology preferred Posting Date 10/12/2026 Closing Date 10/26/2026 Open Until Filled 