    "https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12905": {
      "title": "Director of Fan Experience and Engagement",
      "description": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | Director of Fan Experience and Engagement Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Director of Fan Experience and Engagement Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume Three (3) professional references Posting Details Position Information Posting Number 20270043NE Job Title Director of Fan Experience and Engagement Number of Vacancies 1 About Murray State Located in the West Kentucky region, Murray State University is a public, comprehensive University which offers a low cost of living, low property taxes, and a four-season climate. Murray has a friendly, small-town atmosphere with locally-owned specialty shops and restaurants, an acclaimed community theater, art guild and award-winning public schools. The area is home to Kentucky Lake and Land Between the Lakes, a 170,000-acre National Recreation Area, which offers a wide-range of activities and amenities for residents and visitors alike. Located in close proximity to major cities and nearby access to Interstate 24, Murray is just a few hours from Nashville, St. Louis, Louisville and Memphis. Learn more about Careers at Murray State University. About Murray State Benefits Faculty and staff of Murray State University have access to a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement, tuition waivers, generous paid holidays, vacation, sick, and paid parental leave, as well as many other benefit offerings. Please refer to the Murray State Benefits page for more information. Equal Opportunity Employment Equal Opportunity Employer/AA. Murray State University does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender, identity, sexual orientation, religion, age, veteran status, disability or political or social viewpoint. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. Type of Employment Regular Full-Time If Part Time, Enter Hours Per Week Work Location Murray, KY Employment Term 12 Months Position Type Staff - Non-Exempt (Hourly) Department Athletics Internal Operations Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities Leads and executes fan experience, game atmosphere, game production, and year-round engagement initiatives that strengthen pride, increase attendance, deepen community connections, grow audiences, and cultivate lifelong Racer supporters. Lead and contribute to the planning, development, and execution of fan experience, game atmosphere, game production, and year-round fan-engagement initiatives across Murray State Athletics. Develop detailed game-presentation plans, scripts, production schedules, and run-of-show documents while coordinating entertainment, promotional, recognition, spirit, student-participation, and sponsor elements. Identify, source, schedule, and coordinate halftime performers, in-venue entertainment, promotional participants, and other game-day talent, including direct involvement in advance preparation and event-day execution. Serve as an active event-day leader by coordinating rehearsals, directing assigned personnel, monitoring the presentation, troubleshooting issues in real time, and ensuring the successful execution of each production element. Create memorable experiences that strengthen school pride, deepen community connections, increase repeat engagement, and cultivate lifelong Racer fans. Develop, preserve, and enhance traditions that strengthen the identity of Murray State Athletics and build meaningful connections with students, alumni, fans, and the broader community. Build and execute targeted engagement and audience-growth initiatives designed to increase attendance, broaden participation, strengthen loyalty, and maintain meaningful relationships with fans throughout the year. Develop and directly support student-engagement initiatives in collaboration with student government, campus organizations, residential communities, student-athletes, and other university partners. Create and execute community activities, youth programming, outreach initiatives, and partnerships that expand the reach and relevance of Murray State Athletics. Collaborate with brand, creative, communications, marketing, video, ticketing, operations, spirit programs, campus partners, and the corporate sponsorship team to produce coordinated, brand-consistent experiences and execute in-game sponsorship assets and partner activations. Coordinate the preparation, testing, and event-day readiness of video-board content, game-production elements, fan-experience platforms, promotional materials, and other audience-facing assets. Design, pilot, execute, and evaluate new fan-engagement initiatives, traditions, theme games, promotional concepts, and experiential programs. Provide hands-on support for conference and NCAA championships, athletics special events, external rentals, and non-athletics events held within Murray State Athletics facilities, including applicable presentation, entertainment, promotional, and audience-engagement elements. Recruit, train, schedule, supervise, and evaluate graduate assistants, student interns, temporary personnel, and game-day event staff while working alongside the team during preparation and execution. Manage assigned budgets, promotional purchasing and inventory, annual plans, event calendars, and other operational resources. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Education Requirements Bachelor’s degree required. Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements One year of relevant experience required. Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Posting Date 10/07/2026 Closing Date 10/21/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume Three (3) professional references Hourly Rate/Annual Salary $20.36 (Additional pay dependent upon qualifications) Staff Grade 109 Work Hours Occasional nights, weekends, and special events. Physical Demands Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently have a Bachelor's degree? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Other Document 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
