 apply. Type of Employment Regular Full-Time If Part Time, Enter Hours Per Week Work Location Murray, KY Employment Term 12 Months Position Type Staff - Non-Exempt (Hourly) Department Athletics Internal Operations Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities Provides high-level administrative and operational support to the Men’s and Women’s basketball programs. This position serves as the primary point of contact for internal and external inquiries, manages day-to-day office operations, and assists with scheduling, communications, and event coordination. Responsibilities & Duties Directly partners with the athletic department’s Executive Team to ensure effective communication and collaboration on all men’s and women’s basketball administrative issues Prioritizes and arranges meetings, conferences, and appointments with key departmental units and leadership, while ensuring Head Coach is available as needed. Assists with operational budget planning and fulfillment Assist the head coach in the completion and submission of necessary NCAA Compliance documents Assist with the coordination of recruiting activities, including itineraries, official/unofficial visits, and recruiting mailing in compliance with NCAA rules Process travel paperwork for recruiting, assist with purchasing card statements, and reimbursements for football staff Assist the Athletics Business Office with any needs, including processing invoices, requisitions, and budget tracking as assigned Build, monitor, and communicate calendars of all team activities Could have duties for both home and away contests Support the planning and execution of basketball-related events, such as banquets, alumni functions, and community outreach Serve as the first point of contact for the basketball office, greeting visitors, answering phones, and responding to inquiries Supervise any federal or university student workers Prepare, proofread, and distribute correspondence, reports and meeting materials Maintain departmental records and files Maintain office supplies and overall organization of the basketball administrative space Other duties as assigned Minimum Education Requirements Two years of college. Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements Three years of Administrative experience required. Additional college education and related work experience may be exchanged year-for-year to meet qualifications. Must possess excellent typing, office procedure, organization, interpersonal, and communication skills. Must be able to work with a variety of people. The ability to multi-task is critical. Keyboarding, filing, MS Office Suite programs, office procedures; bookkeeping may be required. Excellent organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree preferred. Posting Date 10/06/2026 Closing Date 10/20/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume Three (3) references Hourly Rate/Annual Salary $15.19 (Additional pay dependent upon qualifications) Staff Grade 103 Work Hours Normal working hours. Physical Demands Normal for office environment. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a minimum of two years of college credit? Yes No * How many years of administrative experience do you have? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Other Document 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
