    "https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12834": {
      "title": "Senior Associate Athletic Director/Chief Revenue Officer",
      "description": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | Senior Associate Athletic Director/Chief Revenue Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Senior Associate Athletic Director/Chief Revenue Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume For best consideration, please submit a completed application along​ with all required materials​ by September 10, 2026.​ Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Job Details Position Information Posting Number 20270009EX Job Title Senior Associate Athletic Director/Chief Revenue Officer Number of Vacancies 1 About Murray State Located in the West Kentucky region, Murray State University is a public, comprehensive University which offers a low cost of living, low property taxes, and a four-season climate. Murray has a friendly, small-town atmosphere with locally-owned specialty shops and restaurants, an acclaimed community theater, art guild and award-winning public schools. The area is home to Kentucky Lake and Land Between the Lakes, a 170,000-acre National Recreation Area, which offers a wide-range of activities and amenities for residents and visitors alike. Located in close proximity to major cities and nearby access to Interstate 24, Murray is just a few hours from Nashville, St. Louis, Louisville and Memphis. Learn more about Careers at Murray State University. About Murray State Benefits Faculty and staff of Murray State University have access to a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement, tuition waivers, generous paid holidays, vacation, sick, and paid parental leave, as well as many other benefit offerings. Please refer to the Murray State Benefits page for more information. Equal Opportunity Employment Equal Opportunity Employer/AA. Murray State University does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender, identity, sexual orientation, religion, age, veteran status, disability or political or social viewpoint. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. Type of Employment Regular Full-Time If Part Time, Enter Hours Per Week Work Location Murray, KY Employment Term 12 Months Position Type Staff - Exempt (Monthly) Department Athletics Internal Operations Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Senior Associate Athletic Director/Chief Revenue Officer serves as a senior leader responsible for advancing revenue generation, philanthropic development, commercial strategy, customer engagement, and business innovation for Murray State Athletics. Reporting directly to the Assistant Vice president & Deputy Director of Athletics/ COO , the Chief Revenue Officer combines strategic thinking with hands-on operational leadership to build scalable revenue systems, optimize institutional assets, strengthen customer and constituent experiences, and position Murray State Athletics for sustainable commercial growth. Lead strategic and operational initiatives spanning ticket sales and service, premium seating, fundraising, membership enhancement, donor engagement, hospitality, customer relationship management, business intelligence, audience monetization, venue utilization, special events, parking and tailgating programs, licensing opportunities, and emerging business ventures. Provide leadership and supervision for assigned revenue-generation and commercial-strategy personnel. Develop and execute an integrated revenue-generation and commercial strategy aligned with the long-term vision, financial sustainability, and competitive ambitions of Murray State Athletics. Lead ticketing strategy and operations across sales, service, retention, pricing, packaging, inventory management, reporting, and customer experience. Develop strategies that grow attendance, improve customer acquisition and retention, strengthen fan loyalty, and increase the long-term value of customer relationships. Develop integrated customer and constituent engagement strategies that strength lifelong relationships with fans, members, donors, partners, and the broader Murray State community. Lead the development, positioning, sales strategy, and performance optimization of premium seating, hospitality products, and other enhanced customer experiences. Develop and execute fundraising strategies that increase philanthropic support while aligning donor engagement initiatives with the long-term priorities of Murray State Athletics. Cultivate meaningful relationships with major gift prospects, donors, alumni, and key stakeholders while supporting a culture of philanthropy throughout the department. Lead membership enhancement initiatives designed to increase participation, strengthen donor acquisition and retention, and expand annual philanthropic support. Oversee donor stewardship, donor services, and constituent engagement practices that deliver exceptional experiences and strengthen long-term donor relationships. Build and oversee customer and constituent relationship management, business intelligence, forecasting, reporting, and revenue-performance systems that strengthen accountability and support informed decision-making. Use pricing strategy, market research, audience segmentation, customer insights, and consumer-behavior data to identify growth opportunities and improve commercial performance. Evaluate athletics facilities, events, programs, experiences, and other institutional assets to identify opportunities for increased utilization, monetization, and enterprise value. Develop and advance special events, external rentals, hospitality programs, parking and tailgating initiatives, licensing opportunities, and other year-round commercial activities. Identify, evaluate and develop new business ventures and nontraditional revenue opportunities consistent with university priorities and the Murray State Athletics brand. Collaborate closely with the corporate sponsorship team to maximize partner value, identify integrated commercial opportunities, and align sponsorship assets with broader revenue and fan-engagement strategies. Collaborate with the Brand, Communications & Fan Engagement unit to align audience growth, campaign priorities, customer acquisition, game-day experiences, and year-round engagement efforts. Partner with athletics leadership, University Advancement, event operations, facilities, finance, development, campus stakeholders, and external partners to ensure coordinated planning and execution across revenue-generating initiatives. Recruit, lead, mentor, and develop assigned staff while establishing clear goals, performance standards, accountability measures, and professional-development opportunities. Monitor trends across collegiate athletics, professional sports, entertainment, hospitality, technology, and consumer engagement to identify emerging opportunities and competitive advantages. Manage assigned budgets, contracts, vendors, operational plans, and departmental resources in accordance with university policies and applicable legal, conference, and NCAA requirements. Review, monitor and manage athletics accounts to ensure accuracy, timely processing, compliance with university, state and NCAA policies, and resolve account issues appropriately. Other duties as assigned. As a member of the Murray State University Athletic Department, you shall comply with all applicable NCAA rules and regulations as provided in the NCAA Division I Manual. If you are found in violation of NCAA regulations, you shall be subject to disciplinary or corrective action as set forth in the provisions of the NCAA enforcement procedures, including suspension without pay or termination of employment for significant or repetitive violations. Minimum Education Requirements Bachelor’s Degree required Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements Two years of experience in revenue generation, fundraising, athletics, account oversight, sales, or high-level administrative experience is required. Demonstrated outstanding organization skills required Demonstrated ability to use Microsoft Excel & Word proficiently Excellent communication skills Strong leadership skills Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications Master’s preferred. Physical Demands Work Hours Occasional nights, weekends and special events. Hourly Rate/Annual Salary Staff Grade 120 Posting Details Posting Date 08/20/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume For best consideration, please submit a completed application along​ with all required materials​ by September 10, 2026.​ Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Other Document 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12833": {
      "title": "Director of Expo Center",
      "description": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | Director of Expo Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Director of Expo Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume For best consideration, please submit a completed application along​ with all required materials​ by September 9, 2026.​ Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Job Details Position Information Posting Number 20270008EX Job Title Director of Expo Center Number of Vacancies 1 About Murray State Located in the West Kentucky region, Murray State University is a public, comprehensive University which offers a low cost of living, low property taxes, and a four-season climate. Murray has a friendly, small-town atmosphere with locally-owned specialty shops and restaurants, an acclaimed community theater, art guild and award-winning public schools. The area is home to Kentucky Lake and Land Between the Lakes, a 170,000-acre National Recreation Area, which offers a wide-range of activities and amenities for residents and visitors alike. Located in close proximity to major cities and nearby access to Interstate 24, Murray is just a few hours from Nashville, St. Louis, Louisville and Memphis. Learn more about Careers at Murray State University. About Murray State Benefits Faculty and staff of Murray State University have access to a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement, tuition waivers, generous paid holidays, vacation, sick, and paid parental leave, as well as many other benefit offerings. Please refer to the Murray State Benefits page for more information. Equal Opportunity Employment Equal Opportunity Employer/AA. Murray State University does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender, identity, sexual orientation, religion, age, veteran status, disability or political or social viewpoint. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. Type of Employment Regular Full-Time If Part Time, Enter Hours Per Week Work Location Murray, KY Employment Term 12 Months Position Type Staff - Exempt (Monthly) Department West KY Expo Ctr Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Expo Director is responsible for the successful operation of the Cherry West Kentucky Livestock and Exposition (Expo) Center, a 2,748 seat multi-event building. Serve as the primary liaison between building users and University staff. Prepare and direct the preparation of marketing/promotional campaigns designed to enhance the facilities’ reputation and maximize usage, as well as making presentations to organizations and groups concerning the capabilities and capacities of the Expo. Establish contractual agreements, overall budgets, operating policies and procedures, as well as identifying operating needs; improve logistics processes and requirements of the facilities. Perform operating and financial analyses to ensure proficiency and optimum realization from assets expended. Meet material/equipment/animal handling requirements, standards for safety for MSU regulations, Fire Marshall Codes, and OSHA . Proactively seek customer satisfaction perceptions and modify goals accordingly. Administer appropriate forms for all inventories, equipment, food accountability, and monitor building and ancillary components. Supervision of the Expo work force of full-time and student employees and training of the Expo work force. Must support and promote the missions of the Huston School of Agriculture and related events and must maintain current promoters/proactively seek new events and have vision to promote Expo to the next level. Oversee the Farm Equipment Training Program in the Hutson School of Agriculture. Directs the supervision of specialists assigned to the various disciplines offered at Expo Center and evaluates the results of specialized programs. Coordinates with the supervisor on appropriate strategies to foster events engaging community aligned with the educational goals supporting the mission of Murray State University. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Education Requirements Bachelor’s degree in agriculture or a field related to the scope of work is required. Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements Must have at least five years of combined experience in the following: Equipment, building, facility and/or farm operation and maintenance. Farm or business management. Show/event leadership in event planning, on-site event management and customer service. Agribusiness Marking/Management Field or Hotel/Restaurant Management. Additional college and related experience may be exchanged year-for-year to meet qualifications. Must be able to show initiative and ability to interface with external customers, agents and event promoters, as well as with MSU Huston School of Agriculture and other departments and personnel on campus. Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications Master’s in agriculture or related field is preferred. Specific experience in exposition-center management. Physical Demands Must be able to physically lift up to 50 pounds for event set-up and operate expo equipment, including tractors, fork lifts, skid steers, telescopic handlers, etc. Work Hours Must be able to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed. Hourly Rate/Annual Salary $48,455 (Additional pay dependent upon qualifications) Staff Grade 113 Posting Details Posting Date 08/19/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume For best consideration, please submit a completed application along​ with all required materials​ by September 9, 2026.​ Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12815": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President for Facilities Management",
      "description": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | Assistant Vice President for Facilities Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Vice President for Facilities Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Greenwood Asher & Associates (GA&A) is assisting Murray State University in this search. Applications and nominations are now being accepted. How to Apply: Please submit application materials through the GA&A candidate portal . Application materials should include: A letter of interest that clearly states the applicant’s qualifications for the position. A current resume/curriculum vitae. Submission of application materials as PDF attachments is strongly encouraged. The search will be conducted with a commitment to confidentiality for candidates until finalists are selected. Initial screening of applications will begin immediately and will continue until an appointment is made. Inquiries and nominations should be directed to: Jeremy Duff Vice President of Executive Search jeremyduff@greenwoodsearch.com Shelley Feather Senior Executive Search Consultant shelleyfeather@greenwoodsearch.com Job Details Position Information Posting Number 20270006EX Job Title Assistant Vice President for Facilities Management Number of Vacancies 1 About Murray State Located in the West Kentucky region, Murray State University is a public, comprehensive University which offers a low cost of living, low property taxes, and a four-season climate. Murray has a friendly, small-town atmosphere with locally-owned specialty shops and restaurants, an acclaimed community theater, art guild and award-winning public schools. The area is home to Kentucky Lake and Land Between the Lakes, a 170,000-acre National Recreation Area, which offers a wide-range of activities and amenities for residents and visitors alike. Located in close proximity to major cities and nearby access to Interstate 24, Murray is just a few hours from Nashville, St. Louis, Louisville and Memphis. Learn more about Careers at Murray State University. About Murray State Benefits Faculty and staff of Murray State University have access to a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement, tuition waivers, generous paid holidays, vacation, sick, and paid parental leave, as well as many other benefit offerings. Please refer to the Murray State Benefits page for more information. Equal Opportunity Employment Equal Opportunity Employer/AA. Murray State University does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender, identity, sexual orientation, religion, age, veteran status, disability or political or social viewpoint. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. Type of Employment Regular Full-Time If Part Time, Enter Hours Per Week Work Location Murray, KY Employment Term 12 Months Position Type Staff - Exempt (Monthly) Department VP for Finance and Admin Services Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities Responsible for assisting the Vice President for Finance and Administrative Services ( VPFAS ) in managing the daily operations and strategic planning of the university facilities. Includes responsibility for all aspects of facility project development and management, as well as direct supervision over the directors and associate directors of Building and Equipment Maintenance, Environmental Safety & Health, Facilities Finance and Administration, Grounds Maintenance and Building Services, Facilities Design & Construction and third-party contracts for grounds and building services. The AVPFM assists in the development and implementation of campus sustainability initiatives, particularly as they relate to energy efficiency and the sustainable design and construction of campus facilities. Responsible for coordinating effective communication and collaboration between campus constituents and project architects, engineers, and the general contractor as well as making frequent presentations to legislative committees and the Board of Regents as required. As head of the University’s Department for Facilities Management, the AVP provides general management, supervision, and professional direction to a comprehensive facilities management organization that provides facilities planning; space administration; architectural and engineering; construction management, facilities maintenance and repair; renovations; utilities generation and distribution; custodial; grounds landscape; recycling; and other maintenance services to the main campus, including Auxiliary Enterprises, the remote facilities of the Breathitt Veterinary Center (veterinary diagnostic center), Regional campus sites in Hopkinsville and Paducah, and Hancock Biological Station. Manages the overall department comprised of a workforce of approximately 65 employees Responsible for an annual budget of approximately $13.5 million and manages an annual renovation volume of $10M (~200+ projects) and major design and construction projects of sometimes near $100 million dollars. Manages contracts for third parties, primarily for custodial and grounds services. Oversees Environmental Safety and Health to ensure adherence to applicable safety rules and health standards, as well as local, state and federal regulations. Develops and recommends policies, planning guidelines, and procedures for the development of the University’s biennial capital budget program, and manages the program throughout the process of development, approval and implementation. Develops and implements, or recommends, University policies and procedures for facilities and utilities systems management, maintenance, operation, and capital construction. Maintains campus master plan and current boundary line information. Maintains land and building data for campus facilities. Responsible for compliance with all federal, state and local building codes and requirements. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Education Requirements Bachelor’s degree in business, engineering, architecture or a related field required. Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements A minimum of eight (8) years of significant experience in roles of progressively increased responsibilities in comprehensive facilities management in an institutional setting, or similar organization setting with multiple, complex systems, of which five years should be in responsible charge of a facilities management organization or a major component of one required. Must have a good working knowledge of facilities planning, design and construction, facilities maintenance and management, utilities operation and management, personnel management and training, and financial management. Must have excellent administrative, supervisory, and oral and written communication skills. Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications Master’s degree in a related field such as engineering, architecture, and construction management Understanding of software for Computerized Maintenance Management System {CMMS) Knowledge of scheduling Software Knowledge of Construction Management software such as Procore Physical Demands Work Hours Hourly Rate/Annual Salary Staff Grade Ungraded Posting Details Posting Date 08/06/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Greenwood Asher & Associates (GA&A) is assisting Murray State University in this search. Applications and nominations are now being accepted. How to Apply: Please submit application materials through the GA&A candidate portal . Application materials should include: A letter of interest that clearly states the applicant’s qualifications for the position. A current resume/curriculum vitae. Submission of application materials as PDF attachments is strongly encouraged. The search will be conducted with a commitment to confidentiality for candidates until finalists are selected. Initial screening of applications will begin immediately and will continue until an appointment is made. Inquiries and nominations should be directed to: Jeremy Duff Vice President of Executive Search jeremyduff@greenwoodsearch.com Shelley Feather Senior Executive Search Consultant shelleyfeather@greenwoodsearch.com Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12793": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Economics",
      "description": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | Assistant Professor, Economics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor, Economics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Curriculum Vitae Copies of graduate transcripts Evidence of teaching effectiveness Recent Research paper (Other Document) Three letters of recommendation will be accessed through the JOE Network. For best consideration, please submit a completed application along​ with all required materials​ by November 8, 2026.​ Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Job Details Position Information Posting Number 20270009FAC Job Title Assistant Professor, Economics Number of Vacancies 1 About Murray State Murray State blends educational opportunities found at research institutions with collaborative interactions among students, faculty and staff found at smaller universities. Students receive personalized attention from supportive faculty and staff as the University offers a 16:1 student-to-faculty ratio. Murray State University places our highest priority on student learning and excellent teaching, blending the range of educational opportunities often experienced at research institutions with the nurturing student-teacher interactions usually found at smaller universities. Located in the West Kentucky region, Murray State University is a public, comprehensive University which offers a low cost of living, low property taxes, and a four-season climate. Murray has a friendly, small-town atmosphere with locally-owned specialty shops and restaurants, an acclaimed community theater, art guild and award-winning public schools. The area is home to Kentucky Lake and Land Between the Lakes, a 170,000-acre National Recreation Area, which offers a wide-range of activities and amenities for residents and visitors alike. Located in close proximity to major cities and nearby access to Interstate 24, Murray is just a few hours from Nashville, St. Louis, Louisville and Memphis. Learn more about Careers at Murray State University. About Murray State Benefits Faculty and staff of Murray State University have access to a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement, tuition waivers, generous paid holidays, vacation, sick, and paid parental leave, as well as many other benefit offerings. Please refer to the Murray State Benefits page for more information. Equal Opportunity Employment Equal Opportunity Employer/AA. Murray State University does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender, identity, sexual orientation, religion, age, veteran status, disability or political or social viewpoint. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. Type of Employment Regular Full-Time If Part Time, Enter Hours Per Week Work Location Murray, KY Employment Term Academic Year Position Type Faculty (Tenure-Track) Department Economics and Finance Anticipated Start Date August 2027 Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities Applicants in all fields of economics will be considered. The successful candidate must demonstrate a commitment to excellent teaching as well as a promising research agenda. The typical course load would be three courses per semester and may include web instruction. Minimum Education Requirements Ph.D. in Economics or a related field is required. ABDs with a documented plan of completion by appointment date will be considered. Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications Physical Demands Work Hours Annual Salary Pay Plan Faculty IV Posting Details Posting Date 07/28/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Curriculum Vitae Copies of graduate transcripts Evidence of teaching effectiveness Recent Research paper (Other Document) Three letters of recommendation will be accessed through the JOE Network. For best consideration, please submit a completed application along​ with all required materials​ by November 8, 2026.​ Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please list a maximum of three courses in order of preference from the following list that in addition to principles you would most likely want to teach based on your qualifications and interests: Behavioral Economics, Business Data Mining, Development Economics, Econometrics, Economic Forecasting, Economics of Sports, Economic Statistics, Environmental Economics, Financial Economics, Game Theory, Health Economics, History of Economic Thought, Industrial Organization, Intermediate Macroeconomics, Intermediate Microeconomics, International Economics, Labor Economics, Law and Economics, Money and Banking, Public Finance, Time Series Econometrics, Urban Economics, Other (please specify). (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Document Copies of Transcripts Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Optional Documents Other Document 2 Other Document 3 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.murraystatejobs.com/postings/12739": {
      "title": "Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Murray State University Applicant Portal Site | Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume For best consideration, please submit a completed application along​ with all required materials​ by August 15, 2026.​ Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Job Details Position Information Posting Number 20270008FAC Job Title Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor Number of Vacancies 1 About Murray State Murray State blends educational opportunities found at research institutions with collaborative interactions among students, faculty and staff found at smaller universities. Students receive personalized attention from supportive faculty and staff as the University offers a 16:1 student-to-faculty ratio. Murray State University places our highest priority on student learning and excellent teaching, blending the range of educational opportunities often experienced at research institutions with the nurturing student-teacher interactions usually found at smaller universities. Located in the West Kentucky region, Murray State University is a public, comprehensive University which offers a low cost of living, low property taxes, and a four-season climate. Murray has a friendly, small-town atmosphere with locally-owned specialty shops and restaurants, an acclaimed community theater, art guild and award-winning public schools. The area is home to Kentucky Lake and Land Between the Lakes, a 170,000-acre National Recreation Area, which offers a wide-range of activities and amenities for residents and visitors alike. Located in close proximity to major cities and nearby access to Interstate 24, Murray is just a few hours from Nashville, St. Louis, Louisville and Memphis. Learn more about Careers at Murray State University. About Murray State Benefits Faculty and staff of Murray State University have access to a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement, tuition waivers, generous paid holidays, vacation, sick, and paid parental leave, as well as many other benefit offerings. Please refer to the Murray State Benefits page for more information. Equal Opportunity Employment Equal Opportunity Employer/AA. Murray State University does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender, identity, sexual orientation, religion, age, veteran status, disability or political or social viewpoint. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. Type of Employment Regular Full-Time If Part Time, Enter Hours Per Week Work Location Hopkinsville, KY Employment Term 12 Months Position Type Faculty (Non-Tenure-Track) Department Breathitt Veterinary Center Anticipated Start Date Summary of Job Duties and Responsibilities Murray State University is seeking a full-time Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor for its Hopkinsville, KY location. The Veterinary Pathologist/Assistant Professor’s primary responsibilities include the following: Perform necropsies on animal carcasses and report appropriate findings. Interpret histopathology slides of necropsy submissions and report findings. Conduct appropriate research and publish findings. Provide consultations with veterinarians and livestock farmers. Provide instruction, as required, for the Animal Health Technology curriculum. Comply with Quality Management System. Perform special projects as determined by Head of Pathology. Minimum Education Requirements Candidates must have Doctor of Veterinary Medicine ( DVM ) or equivalent degree. In addition to the degree, must have 2 years of residency training in anatomic pathology with an emphasis on food animal and companion animal diagnostics. Minimum Experience and Skill Requirements Preferred Education and/or Experience Qualifications American College of Veterinary Pathologists ( ACVP ) Board Certification preferred. Physical Demands Work Hours Up to 5% local travel to present and attend professional meetings. Annual Salary Pay Plan Faculty III Posting Details Posting Date 07/15/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Along with the application, the following items must be included: Letter of application Resume For best consideration, please submit a completed application along​ with all required materials​ by August 15, 2026.​ Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document 412 Sparks Hall Murray, KY 42071 - msu.hr@murraystate.edu - (270) 809-2146 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
